3a:T413,Two streams: (1) the SAP ORDR open backlog, real orders, dated by PROMISE (DocDueDate; measured 2026-08-31: 131 of 138 open docs already overdue, so most enter day 1 — the state of the book, not an assumption); (2) the plan as a FORECAST for demand not yet ordered, net of the backlog: EXIM's weekly buckets where they exist (trade 1,890,300 L), plus the un-bucketed ecom volume (2,433,000 L — EXIM has no ecom weekly split) spread evenly across the month's working days as week 0. ASSUMPTION: the even ecom spread. Stream 2 is a projection, tagged channel=FORECAST so it can be separated on the site. NOT the OMS mirror (dead, unjoinable). SCOPE: the backlog counted here covers the 84 plan SKUs only — open FG orders on non-plan codes are outside the sim's world (it cannot produce them) and are counted separately in opening.backlog_nonplan_*. VALUE BASIS: order value = OpenQty x unit Price, the open pieces' worth — SUM(LineTotal) was refuted (it includes the delivered part of part-shipped lines; Rs 14.4 Cr / 44% overstatement).32:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-8","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-baseline justify-between mb-3","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-lg font-semibold","children":"News of the day"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-xs text-zinc-500","children":[48," PO landings · ",105," real order rows · ",67," forecast rows"]}]]}],[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-3 max-w-4xl text-xs text-zinc-500","children":["Purchase orders landing at the gate are the plan's only external arrivals — each lands when its assumed lead time runs out, and on some days nothing lands. Orders are split hard:"," ",["$","span",null,{"className":"text-zinc-300","children":"real"}]," rows are the measured SAP backlog entering by promise date;"," ",["$","span",null,{"className":"text-sky-300","children":"forecast"}]," rows are the plan wearing a date — nobody has ordered them."]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-4 rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/25 bg-emerald-500/5 p-3 text-sm","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"title":"Pulled from SAP / the factory app on 31 Aug — an observed fact.","className":"inline-block align-middle text-[10px] font-semibold tracking-wider px-1.5 py-px rounded border bg-emerald-500/15 text-emerald-300 border-emerald-500/30","children":"MEASURED"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"font-medium text-emerald-200","children":"Day 1 is a pile, and the pile is real."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-1.5 text-zinc-300","children":"the day-1 order pile is MEASURED reality, not a bug — most of the open backlog was already overdue on 31 Aug."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-1.5 text-xs text-zinc-400","children":["Within the sim's world — the ",84," plan SKUs — the frozen opening carries"," ",["$","span",null,{"className":"tabular-nums","children":47}]," open order documents,"," ",["$","span",null,{"className":"tabular-nums","children":40}]," of them already overdue on 31 Aug. Most of that slice enters as the pile below — the rest enters on later days, by promise date; the whole slice is worth ","₹28.23 Cr"," across ","12,88,754"," pieces. The SAP-wide count is a different, wider fact — quoted in full provenance:"]}],["$","details",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-xs text-zinc-500","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"cursor-pointer text-emerald-300/80 hover:text-emerald-200","children":"the demand stream's full provenance, verbatim"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-2 whitespace-pre-line border-l-2 border-emerald-500/30 pl-3","children":"$3a"}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"grid gap-3 lg:grid-cols-2","children":["$L3b","$L3c"]}],"$L3d"]]}]
